{"name":"Solitaire","hex":"#c6decf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"solitaire","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who lives alone; a recluse or hermit.","A game for one person, played on a board with pegs or balls, in which the object is, beginning with all the places filled except one, to remove all but one of the pieces by \"jumping\", as in draughts."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Living or being alone; solitary."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solitaire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Solitaire","blocks":[{"text":"Solitaire, patience, or card solitaire refer to a genre of card games whose common feature is that the aim is to arrange the cards in some systematic order or, in a few cases, to pair them off in order to discard them. Most are intended for play by a single player, but there are varieties for two or more players."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Carpet_patience_1.jpg/330px-Carpet_patience_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solitaire","wikidata":"Q2056928"},{"title":"Solitaire (Neil Sedaka song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Solitaire\" is a ballad composed by Neil Sedaka with lyrics by Phil Cody and originally recorded by Sedaka on his 1972 album Solitaire. It uses the card game of solitaire as a metaphor for a man \"who lost his love through his indifference\"—\"while life goes on around him everywhere he's playing solitaire\". A version by Andy Williams reached number 4 in the UK Singles Chart in 1973. In 1975, the song was a U.S. top-20 single for the Carpenters."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Searchers_Solitaire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solitaire_(Neil_Sedaka_song)","wikidata":"Q7558181"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Patience_cards.jpg/250px-Patience_cards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a7/Patience_cards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Patience_cards.jpg/250px-Patience_cards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Patience-sized playing cards (bottom) are smaller than regular playing cards (top); this is because a game where cards are laid out may take up a large amount of table space[11]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APatience_cards.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/KPatience.png/500px-KPatience.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/KPatience.png/500px-KPatience.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Klondike, often simply called \"Solitaire\" by software producers.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKPatience.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c6/Andy_williams-solitaire_s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c6/Andy_williams-solitaire_s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAndy_williams-solitaire_s.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a4/CarpsSolitare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a4/CarpsSolitare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarpsSolitare.jpg"}],"sound